 "recognition_note": "The exact supplied 21-residue HCDR3 matches CBH-4G in Ogishi et al. Supplementary Dataset 1 (Scientific Reports, 2016-07-12). I confirmed the row and sequence on 2026-10-29. No native CBH-4G-E2 complex was found or inspected; no full published paired VH/VL sequence was found, so recognition rests on the exact long HCDR3 plus antigen context.",
 "what_separated_them": "Tier A was available: exact-HCDR3 recognition makes CBH-4G's conformational domain-A/non-neutralizing phenotype relevant, separating the back-face candidates from receptor-face candidates. The CBH-4G-specific Y632NS affinity loss transfers exactly to C:225 but supports both overlapping C4 and C8. Candidate-neutral geometry then separated them: C4 is a compact connected patch centered on C:225 (12/17 residues within 10 Å, no internal sequon), whereas C8 is 31.39 Å wide, only 3/10 residues are within 10 Å, and it includes a buried residue and a sequon. Generic accessibility and chemistry did not decide the order.",
